      "body": "## Problem\n\n`test/python/core/graph/test_native_backend_lowering.py::test_native_sdpa_fwd_lowers_to_backend` builds a causal f16 SDPA graph and asserts that it ran on the cuDNN backend plan (`_assert_ran_on_backend`). The FROST SDPA forward prefill engines are default candidates: `sdpa_fwd_prefill_sm80`, `_sm90`, `_sm100`, `_sm107` and `_sm120` carry no `opt_in` in `engines/manifest.py`. Where the heuristics rank one of them first, it claims the graph and the test fails:\n\n```\nassert FrostSdpaFwdEngine(name='sdpa_fwd_prefill_sm120', engine_id=20505) is None\n```\n\n| GPU | develop |\n|---|---|\n| RTX 5060 Ti (cc 12.0) | fails |\n| B300 (cc 10.3) | fails |\n| A100 (cc 8.0) | passes (the backend ranks first) |\n| GH200 (cc 9.0) | passes (the backend ranks first) |\n\n## Change\n\n#2115 made the same change for the norm tests in this file (`_bar_frost_norm`). This PR does the same for SDPA:\n- `_bar_frost_sdpa_fwd(g)` bars the `frost_sdpa_fwd` family by name;\n- the test builds through it.\n\nThe test keeps covering the generic lowering to the backend, which is what it is for. FROST SDPA keeps its own suites under `test/python/sdpa/frost`. The benchmarks already bar FROST SDPA the same way on their backend legs (`benchmark_single_sdpa.py`, `benchmark_single_attention.py`).\n\n## Testing\n\n`test/python/core/graph/test_native_backend_lowering.py`, develop `a0f7b9f4`, cuDNN 9.27:\n\n| GPU | develop | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| RTX 5060 Ti (cc 12.0) | `test_native_sdpa_fwd_lowers_to_backend` fails | 17 passed, 4 skipped |\n| A100 (cc 8.0) | passes | 16 passed, 5 skipped |\n\n`black 26.3.1 --line-length 160 --fast` is clean.\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
