            "body": "A correction on the cc 10.3 row of the table. The B300 failure I cited came from runs with `CUDNN_FRONTEND_ENABLE_FROST_ENGINES=1`. In a default run (FROST engines off), `test/python/core` passes on B300: 512 passed, 0 failed. On cc 12.0 the test fails in the default run too, which is the case the PR body measures. The bar is correct either way. It just stops the test depending on whether a FROST SDPA engine wins the ranking.",
