            "body": "**Codex bot review · model: `gpt-6-astra`**\n\nReviewed `7c6c08ce8736` against base `a0f7b9f4e8e3`.\n\nThank you for your contribution! No actionable findings. The exclusion uses the manifest's SDPA-forward family, and the test retains its backend-plan and numerical assertions. Production engine selection is unchanged.\n\nValidation: All 21 backend-lowering tests passed on native SM100 with cuDNN 9.26 and normal engine opt-in settings. With opt-in engines enabled, removing the new exclusion selected sdpa_fwd_prefill_sm100 and failed the backend assertion. Restoring it selected the backend, created and built backend plans, and passed the SDPA numerical comparison. With normal settings, both variants selected the backend on this device. Precheck found no candidates.\n\nLimitations: No native SM103 or SM120 run was available. The covering python/misc CI route remains on access hold. Style and Security workflows require maintainer approval.\n\nApproved: no P0 or high-risk P1 found. Remaining findings stay with the owner; merge timing stays with the owner.\n\n<!-- codex-fe-review:v2:2233:7c6c08ce8736358ca995aaa8c0b6801a3e859799:complete:no-blocker -->",
